# RPM build install notes

These instructions create a source tarball in the layout expected by
`rpm/geoipsets.spec`, copy all RPM source files into the RPM `SOURCES`
directory, and build the RPM.

The spec currently packages this Git snapshot:

```text
commit: fdc367fade27b946f7694423f61add42359e031b
version: 2.4.0
release: 0.1.20260506gitfdc367f
```

If you build from a different commit, update the `commit`, `shortcommit`, and
`snapdate` macros at the top of `rpm/geoipsets.spec`.

## Install build tools

On Fedora:

```bash
sudo dnf install rpm-build rpmdevtools python3-devel pyproject-rpm-macros systemd-rpm-macros
```

## Prepare rpmbuild directories

```bash
rpmdev-setuptree
```

If `rpmdev-setuptree` is not available, create the directories manually:

```bash
mkdir -p ~/rpmbuild/{BUILD,BUILDROOT,RPMS,SOURCES,SPECS,SRPMS}
```

## Create the source tarball with --transform

Run these commands from the repository root. The final `.` is required; it is
the directory that tar should add to the archive.

```bash
repo_root="$(pwd)"
sources_dir="${HOME}/rpmbuild/SOURCES"
commit="$(git -C "${repo_root}" rev-parse HEAD)"
shortcommit="${commit:0:7}"
tarball="${sources_dir}/geoipsets-${shortcommit}.tar.gz"

mkdir -p "${sources_dir}"

tar -C "${repo_root}" \
  --exclude=.git \
  --exclude=rpm/build \
  --transform "s,^\.,geoipsets-${commit}," \
  -czf "${tarball}" .
```

The `--transform` option puts every file under the top-level directory expected
by the spec:

```text
geoipsets-fdc367fade27b946f7694423f61add42359e031b/
```

That directory name must match the `%autosetup -n %{name}-%{commit}` line in
`rpm/geoipsets.spec`.

## Copy required RPM sources

The tarball is already created directly in `~/rpmbuild/SOURCES`. Put the
additional `Source` files there too:

```bash
install -pm 0644 rpm/geoipsets.conf "${sources_dir}/geoipsets.conf"
install -pm 0644 rpm/update-geoipsets.service "${sources_dir}/update-geoipsets.service"
install -pm 0644 rpm/update-geoipsets.timer "${sources_dir}/update-geoipsets.timer"
install -pm 0644 rpm/geoipsets.tmpfiles "${sources_dir}/geoipsets.tmpfiles"
```

Copy the spec into `~/rpmbuild/SPECS`:

```bash
cp rpm/geoipsets.spec ~/rpmbuild/SPECS/
```

## Build the RPM

```bash
rpmbuild -ba ~/rpmbuild/SPECS/geoipsets.spec
```

Build outputs will be written below:

```text
~/rpmbuild/RPMS/
~/rpmbuild/SRPMS/
```

## One-command helper

The helper script performs the same staging steps under `~/rpmbuild` by default:

```bash
./rpm/build-rpm.sh
```

It creates the tarball with `tar --transform`, copies the config, systemd, and
tmpfiles sources, then runs `rpmbuild -ba`.

To use a different RPM build root, set `RPM_TOPDIR`:

```bash
RPM_TOPDIR=/path/to/rpmbuild ./rpm/build-rpm.sh
```
